== A. First Look

=== S001 · First Look Q1 Call-option convexity arbitrage / 看涨期权凸性套利 （Page 1）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 某不派息资产现价为 $\$22$，期限均为九个月、执行价分别为 $\$20$ 与 $\$25$ 的看涨期权价格为 $\$5.50$ 与 $\$1$。构造一个套利组合。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> A non-dividend-paying asset is at $\$22$. Nine-month calls with strikes $\$20$ and $\$25$ trade at $\$5.50$ and $\$1$. Find an arbitrage.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Treat the stock as a zero-strike call. Buy one share and four $K=25$ calls, and short five $K=20$ calls. The initial cash flow is</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$5(5.50)-22-4(1)=1.50>0.$$</p>
<p>At expiry the payoff is $S_T$ for $S_T\le20$, $100-4S_T\ge0$ for $20&lt;S_T\le25$, and $0$ for $S_T&gt;25$. The portfolio therefore produces cash today and can never have a negative terminal payoff.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S002 · First Look Q2 Eigenvalues of a correlation matrix / 相关矩阵的特征值 （Page 1）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> （i）$n$ 个随机变量的相关矩阵，其特征值之和是多少？（ii）若该相关矩阵非奇异，其逆矩阵的特征值之和至少是多少？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> (i) What is the sum of the eigenvalues of an $n\times n$ correlation matrix? (ii) Give a lower bound for the sum of the eigenvalues of its inverse when the correlation matrix is nonsingular.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>The sum is the trace, hence $\sum_i\lambda_i=n$. Nonsingularity makes every $\lambda_i&gt;0$, and Cauchy–Schwarz gives</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\left(\sum_{i=1}^n\lambda_i\right)\left(\sum_{i=1}^n\lambda_i^{-1}\right)\ge n^2.$$</p>
<p>Therefore $\sum_i\lambda_i^{-1}\ge n$, with equality exactly when all eigenvalues are $1$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S003 · First Look Q3 Integrated Brownian motion / 布朗运动的时间积分 （Page 1）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 设 $W_t$ 为 Wiener 过程，$X_t=\int_0^t W_s\,ds$。求 $X_t$ 的分布，并判断 $\{X_t\}$ 是否为鞅。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Let $W_t$ be a Wiener process and $X_t=\int_0^t W_s\,ds$. Find the distribution of $X_t$ and decide whether $X_t$ is a martingale.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Stochastic Fubini gives $X_t=\int_0^t(t-s)\,dW_s$, so</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$X_t\sim N\!\left(0,\int_0^t(t-s)^2ds\right)=N\!\left(0,\frac{t^3}{3}\right).$$</p>
<p>It is not a martingale: for $u&gt;t$, $\mathbb E[X_u\mid\mathcal F_t]=X_t+(u-t)W_t$, which is generally different from $X_t$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S004 · First Look Q4 Flipping blocks in a bit matrix / 翻转二进制矩阵方块 （Page 1）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 一个 $8\times8$ 矩阵只含 $0$ 和 $1$。每次可选任意 $3\times3$ 或 $4\times4$ 子块，将其中所有位翻转。是否总能把任意初始矩阵变成全零矩阵？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> An $8\times8$ matrix contains only zeroes and ones. Each move flips every bit in any chosen $3\times3$ or $4\times4$ block. Can every initial matrix be changed into the all-zero matrix?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>No. There are $6^2=36$ possible $3\times3$ blocks and $5^2=25$ possible $4\times4$ blocks. Because flips commute and repeating a flip cancels it, at most $2^{36+25}=2^{61}$ matrices are reachable from zero. There are $2^{64}$ binary $8\times8$ matrices, so at least one—and therefore many—cannot be reached. Reversibility gives the same conclusion for reducing arbitrary matrices to zero.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S005 · First Look Q5 Completing a correlation matrix / 补全相关矩阵 （Page 2）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 求所有使下列矩阵成为相关矩阵的 $\rho$：
$$\begin{pmatrix}1&0.6&-0.3\\0.6&1&\rho\\-0.3&\rho&1\end{pmatrix}.$$</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Find every $\rho$ for which
$$\begin{pmatrix}1&0.6&-0.3\\0.6&1&\rho\\-0.3&\rho&1\end{pmatrix}$$
is a correlation matrix.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>The matrix must be positive semidefinite. Its only binding principal-minor condition is</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\det R=0.55-0.36\rho-\rho^2\ge0.$$</p>
<p>Hence</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{\frac{-9-4\sqrt{91}}{50}\le\rho\le\frac{-9+4\sqrt{91}}{50}} \approx[-0.9432,0.5832].$$</p>
<p>The endpoints are included: they give valid singular correlation matrices.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S006 · First Look Q6 Sampling a narrow uniform interval / 均匀抽样命中小区间 （Page 2）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 至少要生成多少个相互独立的 $U[0,1]$ 随机变量，才能以不低于 $95\%$ 的概率保证至少有一个落在 $[0.70,0.72]$？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How many independent $U[0,1]$ variables are needed so that at least one lies in $[0.70,0.72]$ with probability at least $95\%$?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>For $N$ draws the hit probability is $1-0.98^N$. Thus</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$N\ge\frac{\log(0.05)}{\log(0.98)}\approx148.28.$$</p>
<p>The smallest integer is therefore $\boxed{149}$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S007 · First Look Q7 The M&M cancellation game / M&M 配对消除游戏 （Page 2）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 袋中六种颜色的 M&amp;M 数量可视为均匀且无限。逐颗抽取：若新糖与桌上某颗同色，就吃掉这两颗；否则把新糖放在桌上。桌上同时出现六种颜色时结束。期望共吃掉多少颗？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> M&amp;M colors are uniformly distributed among six colors. Draw repeatedly; a draw matching a color already on the table causes both candies of that color to be eaten, while a new color remains on the table. Stop when all six colors are present. What is the expected number eaten?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Let $A_n$ be the expected candies eaten while moving from $n$ displayed colors to $n+1$. For $1\le n\le5$, a match has probability $n/6$ and returns the process to $n-1$, so</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$A_n=\frac n6(2+A_{n-1}+A_n),\qquad A_0=0.$$</p>
<p>This gives $(A_1,\ldots,A_5)=(2/5,6/5,16/5,52/5,62)$. Hence the answer is</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\sum_{n=0}^5A_n=\boxed{\frac{386}{5}=77.2}.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S008 · First Look Q8 South, east, north / 向南、向东、向北 （Page 2）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 在球形地球表面从某点出发，向南、向东、向北各走一英里后回到起点。若起点不是北极，它还可能在哪里？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> On a spherical Earth, walk one mile south, one mile east, and one mile north and return to the starting point. Apart from the North Pole, where can the starting point be?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>For every positive integer $k$, take a latitude near the South Pole whose circumference is $1/k$ mile, and start one mile north of it. The southward leg reaches that latitude, the eastward mile completes exactly $k$ circuits, and the northward leg retraces the first leg. Every point on each such starting latitude works.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S009 · First Look Q9 Ornstein–Uhlenbeck SDE / Ornstein–Uhlenbeck 随机微分方程 （Page 3）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 求解
$$dr_t=\lambda(\theta-r_t)\,dt+\sigma\,dW_t,\qquad \lambda&gt;0.$$</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Solve the Ornstein–Uhlenbeck equation
$$dr_t=\lambda(\theta-r_t)\,dt+\sigma\,dW_t,\qquad \lambda&gt;0.$$</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Multiplying by $e^{\lambda t}$ and integrating yields</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$r_t=\theta+(r_0-\theta)e^{-\lambda t}+\sigma\int_0^t e^{-\lambda(t-s)}\,dW_s.$$</p>
<p>Consequently $r_t$ is normal with mean $\theta+(r_0-\theta)e^{-\lambda t}$ and variance $\sigma^2(1-e^{-2\lambda t})/(2\lambda)$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S010 · First Look Q10 A symmetric integral / 对称积分 （Page 3）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 若积分存在，求
$$\int_0^a\frac{f(x)}{f(x)+f(a-x)}\,dx.$$</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Assuming the integral exists, evaluate
$$\int_0^a\frac{f(x)}{f(x)+f(a-x)}\,dx.$$</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Substitute $x\mapsto a-x$. The transformed integrand is $f(a-x)/(f(a-x)+f(x))$. Adding the original and transformed integrals makes the integrand equal to $1$, so twice the required integral is $a$. The value is $\boxed{a/2}$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S011 · First Look Q11 Signs of correlated normals / 相关正态变量的符号 （Page 3）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> $X,Y$ 为相关系数 $\rho$ 的联合标准正态变量。求 $\mathbb E[\operatorname{sgn}(X)\operatorname{sgn}(Y)]$。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Let $X,Y$ be jointly standard normal with correlation $\rho$. Find $\mathbb E[\operatorname{sgn}(X)\operatorname{sgn}(Y)]$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>The Gaussian quadrant formula is</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$P(X&gt;0,Y&gt;0)=\frac14+\frac{\arcsin\rho}{2\pi}.$$</p>
<p>Equal signs contribute $1$ and opposite signs contribute $-1$, hence</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{\mathbb E[\operatorname{sgn}(X)\operatorname{sgn}(Y)]=\frac{2}{\pi}\arcsin\rho}.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S012 · First Look Q12 Long gamma and short vega / 多 Gamma、空 Vega （Page 3）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何用期权构造一个 Gamma 为正、Vega 为负的组合？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How can an options portfolio be made long gamma but short vega?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Buy shorter-dated options and sell a suitable quantity of otherwise comparable longer-dated options. In Black–Scholes, $\nu=S^2\sigma T\Gamma$, so the longer maturity has more vega per unit of gamma. If $T_s&lt;T_\ell$, choose long and short quantities so that</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\frac{\Gamma_sT_s}{\Gamma_\ell T_\ell}q_s&lt;q_\ell&lt;\frac{\Gamma_s}{\Gamma_\ell}q_s.$$</p>
<p>Then $q_s\Gamma_s-q_\ell\Gamma_\ell&gt;0$ while $q_s\nu_s-q_\ell\nu_\ell&lt;0$. Strikes and notionals must be selected using the actual Greeks.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S013 · First Look Q13 Ratio of geometric Brownian motions / 两个几何布朗运动之比 （Page 3）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 设
$$\frac{dX_t}{X_t}=\mu_Xdt+\sigma_XdW_t,\qquad
\frac{dY_t}{Y_t}=\mu_Ydt+\sigma_YdB_t,$$
且 $d\langle W,B\rangle_t=\rho\,dt$。证明 $Z_t=X_t/Y_t$ 仍是几何布朗运动，并求其漂移与波动率。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Let $X_t$ and $Y_t$ be geometric Brownian motions with coefficients $(\mu_X,\sigma_X)$ and $(\mu_Y,\sigma_Y)$, driven by Brownian motions of correlation $\rho$. Show that $Z_t=X_t/Y_t$ is a geometric Brownian motion and identify its drift and volatility.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Itô's formula gives</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\frac{dZ_t}{Z_t}=
\bigl(\mu_X-\mu_Y+\sigma_Y^2-\rho\sigma_X\sigma_Y\bigr)dt
+\sigma_XdW_t-\sigma_YdB_t.$$</p>
<p>The last two terms equal $\sigma_Zd\widetilde W_t$, where</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\sigma_Z=\sqrt{\sigma_X^2+\sigma_Y^2-2\rho\sigma_X\sigma_Y}.$$</p>
<p>Thus $Z$ is a GBM with the displayed drift and volatility.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S014 · First Look Q14 The k-th largest array element / 数组中第 k 大元素 （Page 4）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 在未排序数组中找第 $k$ 大元素；重复值按排序后的位置计数，而不是按不同数值计数。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Find the $k$-th largest element of an unsorted array. Count positions in sorted order, not distinct values.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Run randomized Quickselect for zero-based target index $n-k$. Partition around a random pivot; recurse only into the side containing the target. Its expected running time is $O(n)$ and in-place extra space is $O(1)$, while the worst case is $O(n^2)$. A deterministic median-of-medians pivot gives worst-case $O(n)$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S015 · First Look Q15 Sliding-window maximum / 滑动窗口最大值 （Page 4）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 给定数组与合法窗口长度 $k$，窗口每次右移一位；返回每个窗口中的最大值。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Given an array and a valid window size $k$, move the window one position at a time and return the maximum in every window.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Maintain a deque of indices whose values are decreasing. Before inserting index $i$, remove expired indices from the front and indices with values no larger than $a_i$ from the back. The front is then the current maximum. Every index enters and leaves once, so time is $O(n)$ and space is $O(k)$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

