== B. Mathematics, Calculus & Differential Equations

=== S016 · Q2.1.1 The value of $i^i$ / $i^i$ 的值 （Page 33）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 设 $i=\sqrt{-1}$，求 $i^i$。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What is $i^i$, where $i=\sqrt{-1}$?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Using the multivalued logarithm, $\log i=i(\pi/2+2\pi k)$, so</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$i^i=e^{i\log i}=e^{-\pi/2-2\pi k},\qquad k\in\mathbb Z.$$</p>
<p>The principal value is $\boxed{e^{-\pi/2}}$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S017 · Q2.1.2 Compare two exponential constants / 比较两个指数常数 （Page 33）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> $\pi^e$ 与 $e^\pi$ 哪个更大？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Which is larger, $\pi^e$ or $e^\pi$?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>The function $f(x)=\log x/x$ is decreasing for $x&gt;e$. Since $\pi&gt;e$, $\log\pi/\pi&lt;1/e$. Multiplication by $e\pi$ gives $e\log\pi&lt;\pi$, hence $\boxed{\pi^e&lt;e^\pi}$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S018 · Q2.1.3 Exponential AM–GM inequality / 指数形式的均值不等式 （Page 33）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 证明对任意 $x,y\in\mathbb R$，
$$\frac{e^x+e^y}{2}\ge e^{(x+y)/2}.$$</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Show that $(e^x+e^y)/2\ge e^{(x+y)/2}$ for all real $x,y$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Apply AM–GM to the positive numbers $e^x$ and $e^y$:</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\frac{e^x+e^y}{2}\ge\sqrt{e^xe^y}=e^{(x+y)/2}.$$</p>
<p>Equality holds exactly when $x=y$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S019 · Q2.1.4 Solve $x^6=64$ / 求解六次方程 （Page 33）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 在复数范围内求解 $x^6=64$。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Solve $x^6=64$ over the complex numbers.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>The six roots are</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{x_k=2e^{i\pi k/3}},\qquad k=0,1,\ldots,5.$$</p>
<p>The two real roots are $2$ and $-2$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S020 · Q2.1.5 Differentiate $x^x$ / 求 $x^x$ 的导数 （Page 33）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 求 $x^x$ 的导数。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Differentiate $x^x$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>For $x&gt;0$, write $x^x=e^{x\log x}$. Therefore</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{\frac{d}{dx}x^x=x^x(\log x+1)}.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S021 · Q2.1.6 An infinite nested radical / 无限嵌套根式 （Page 33）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 计算
$$\sqrt{2+\sqrt{2+\sqrt{2+\cdots}}}.$$</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Evaluate $\sqrt{2+\sqrt{2+\sqrt{2+\cdots}}}$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>If the positive limit is $L$, then $L=\sqrt{2+L}$, so $L^2-L-2=0$ and $L=2$. The finite truncations increase and are bounded above by $2$, which justifies taking the limit. Thus the value is $\boxed{2}$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S022 · Q2.1.7 An infinite power tower / 无限幂塔 （Page 33）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 求 $x$，使无限幂塔满足
$$x^{x^{x^{\cdot^{\cdot^\cdot}}}}=2.$$</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Find $x$ such that the convergent infinite power tower $x^{x^{x^{\cdot^{\cdot^\cdot}}}}$ equals $2$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>If the tower has limit $L=2$, then $x^L=L$, giving $x^2=2$. The positive candidate is $x=\sqrt2$, and it lies in the convergence interval $[e^{-e},e^{1/e}]$. Hence $\boxed{x=\sqrt2}$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S023 · Q2.1.8 Three infinite series / 三个无穷级数 （Page 33）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 判断下列级数的敛散性：
$$\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac1k,\qquad
\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac1{k^2},\qquad
\sum_{k=2}^{\infty}\frac1{k\log k}.$$</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Determine which of $\sum1/k$, $\sum1/k^2$, and $\sum_{k\ge2}1/(k\log k)$ converge.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>The harmonic series diverges. The $p$-series with $p=2$ converges. The third diverges by the integral test because</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\int_2^N\frac{dx}{x\log x}=\log\log N-\log\log2\longrightarrow\infty.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S024 · Q2.1.9 An arctangent integral / 反正切积分 （Page 34）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 计算 $\int(1+x^2)^{-1}\,dx$。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Compute $\int dx/(1+x^2)$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{\int\frac{dx}{1+x^2}=\arctan x+C}.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S025 · Q2.1.10 Two integrations by parts / 两个分部积分 （Page 34）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 计算 $\int x\log x\,dx$ 与 $\int xe^x\,dx$。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Compute $\int x\log x\,dx$ and $\int xe^x\,dx$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Integration by parts gives</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{\int x\log x\,dx=\frac{x^2}{2}\log x-\frac{x^2}{4}+C},$$</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{\int xe^x\,dx=e^x(x-1)+C}.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S026 · Q2.1.11 A logarithmic integration-by-parts formula / 对数分部积分公式 （Page 34）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 计算 $\int x^n\log x\,dx$。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Compute $\int x^n\log x\,dx$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>For $n\ne-1$,</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{\int x^n\log x\,dx=
x^{n+1}\left(\frac{\log x}{n+1}-\frac1{(n+1)^2}\right)+C}.$$</p>
<p>For $n=-1$, the value is $\tfrac12(\log x)^2+C$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S027 · Q2.1.12 Powers of logarithms / 对数幂的积分 （Page 34）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 对非负整数 $n$，计算 $\int(\log x)^n\,dx$。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> For a nonnegative integer $n$, compute $\int(\log x)^n\,dx$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Let $I_n=\int(\log x)^n dx$. Integration by parts gives $I_n=x(\log x)^n-nI_{n-1}$ and $I_0=x$. Therefore</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{I_n=x\sum_{k=0}^{n}(-1)^k\frac{n!}{(n-k)!}(\log x)^{n-k}+C}.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S028 · Q2.1.13 A second-order ODE / 二阶常微分方程 （Page 34）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 求解 $y''-4y'+4y=1$。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Solve $y''-4y'+4y=1$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>The characteristic polynomial is $(r-2)^2$, and a constant particular solution is $1/4$. Thus</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{y(x)=(C_1+C_2x)e^{2x}+\frac14}.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S029 · Q2.1.14 The logistic ODE / Logistic 方程 （Page 34）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 求所有满足 $f'(x)=f(x)(1-f(x))$ 的函数。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Find all solutions of $f'(x)=f(x)(1-f(x))$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>The nonconstant solutions follow by separation:</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{f(x)=\frac{1}{1+Ce^{-x}}}.$$</p>
<p>On any interval where the denominator is nonzero, this solves the equation. The constant solutions are $f\equiv0$ and $f\equiv1$; the latter is included by $C=0$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S030 · Q2.1.15 Derive the Black–Scholes PDE / 推导 Black–Scholes 方程 （Page 34）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 推导 Black–Scholes 偏微分方程。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Derive the Black–Scholes PDE.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Let $dS_t=\mu S_tdt+\sigma S_tdW_t$ and $V=V(t,S)$. Itô's lemma gives</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$dV=\left(V_t+\mu SV_S+\frac12\sigma^2S^2V_{SS}\right)dt+\sigma SV_SdW.$$</p>
<p>In the delta-hedged portfolio $\Pi=V-V_SS$, the diffusion cancels. No arbitrage requires $d\Pi=r\Pi\,dt$. After cancellation of $\mu$ this becomes</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{V_t+\frac12\sigma^2S^2V_{SS}+rSV_S-rV=0}.$$</p>
<p>With continuous dividend yield $q$, replace $rS V_S$ by $(r-q)S V_S$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="section-anchor" id="stefanica-linear-algebra" aria-hidden="true"></div>
~~~

== C. Covariance, Correlation & Linear Algebra

=== S031 · Q2.2.1 Covariance matrices are positive semidefinite / 协方差矩阵半正定 （Page 35）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 证明任意协方差矩阵都是对称半正定矩阵，并说明相关矩阵为何也如此。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Show that every covariance matrix is symmetric positive semidefinite, and show the same for correlation matrices.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>For a random vector $X$ with covariance matrix $\Sigma$ and any deterministic $a$,</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$a^\top\Sigma a=\operatorname{Var}(a^\top X)\ge0.$$</p>
<p>Also $\Sigma_{ij}=\operatorname{Cov}(X_i,X_j)=\Sigma_{ji}$. A correlation matrix is $R=D^{-1/2}\Sigma D^{-1/2}$, so $a^\top Ra=(D^{-1/2}a)^\top\Sigma(D^{-1/2}a)\ge0$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S032 · Q2.2.2 Convert covariance to correlation / 从协方差矩阵得到相关矩阵 （Page 35）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 已知
$$\Sigma=\begin{pmatrix}1&0.36&-1.44\\0.36&4&0.80\\-1.44&0.80&9\end{pmatrix},$$
求相关矩阵。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Find the correlation matrix corresponding to
$$\Sigma=\begin{pmatrix}1&0.36&-1.44\\0.36&4&0.80\\-1.44&0.80&9\end{pmatrix}.$$</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>The standard deviations are $1,2,3$. Divide $\Sigma_{ij}$ by $\sigma_i\sigma_j$:</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{R=\begin{pmatrix}
1&0.18&-0.48\\
0.18&1&2/15\\
-0.48&2/15&1
\end{pmatrix}}.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S033 · Q2.2.3 Equicorrelation bounds / 等相关系数的范围 （Page 35）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 一个 $n\times n$ 相关矩阵的所有非对角元素都等于 $\rho$。求 $\rho$ 的取值范围。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Every off-diagonal entry of an $n\times n$ correlation matrix equals $\rho$. Find the possible range of $\rho$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>The eigenvalues are $1-\rho$ with multiplicity $n-1$ and $1+(n-1)\rho$ once. Positive semidefiniteness is therefore equivalent to</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{-\frac1{n-1}\le\rho\le1}.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S034 · Q2.2.4 How many eigenvalues and eigenvectors? / 特征值与特征向量有多少 （Page 35）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 一个实 $n\times n$ 矩阵有多少个特征值、多少个特征向量？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How many eigenvalues and eigenvectors does a real $n\times n$ matrix have?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Over $\mathbb C$, the characteristic polynomial has exactly $n$ roots counted with algebraic multiplicity; nonreal roots of a real matrix occur in conjugate pairs. Over $\mathbb R$ there may be no real eigenvalue when $n$ is even. There are infinitely many eigenvectors whenever an eigenvalue exists, because every nonzero scalar multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector. What is bounded by $n$ is the number of <em>linearly independent</em> eigenvectors; it equals $n$ exactly when the matrix is diagonalizable.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S035 · Q2.2.5 Matrix square root and Cholesky factor / 矩阵平方根与 Cholesky 分解 （Page 35）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 设
$$A=\begin{pmatrix}2&-2\\-2&5\end{pmatrix}.$$
（i）求 $M$ 使 $M^2=A$；（ii）求 $M$ 使 $A=MM^\top$。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> For $A=\begin{pmatrix}2&-2\\-2&5\end{pmatrix}$, (i) find $M$ with $M^2=A$; (ii) find $M$ with $A=MM^\top$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>The eigenvalues of $A$ are $1$ and $6$, with orthogonal eigenvectors $(2,1)^\top$ and $(1,-2)^\top$. Its principal square root is</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{A^{1/2}=\frac15\begin{pmatrix}
4+\sqrt6&2-2\sqrt6\\
2-2\sqrt6&1+4\sqrt6
\end{pmatrix}}.$$</p>
<p>A lower-triangular Cholesky factor is</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{M=\begin{pmatrix}\sqrt2&0\\-\sqrt2&\sqrt3\end{pmatrix}},\qquad A=MM^\top.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S036 · Q2.2.6 Apply a matrix from its eigenvectors / 利用特征向量计算矩阵作用 （Page 36）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> $A$ 的特征值为 $2,-3$，对应特征向量分别为 $(1,2)^\top,(-1,3)^\top$。若 $v=(3,1)^\top$，求 $Av$。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Matrix $A$ has eigenvalues $2,-3$ with eigenvectors $(1,2)^\top,(-1,3)^\top$. For $v=(3,1)^\top$, find $Av$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Decompose $v=2(1,2)^\top-(-1,3)^\top$. Therefore</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$Av=2\cdot2(1,2)^\top+(-3)(-1)(-1,3)^\top=\boxed{(1,17)^\top}.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S037 · Q2.2.7 Trace of $AB$ and $BA$ / $AB$ 与 $BA$ 的迹 （Page 36）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 对同阶方阵 $A,B$，证明 $\operatorname{tr}(AB)=\operatorname{tr}(BA)$。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> For square matrices $A,B$ of the same size, prove $\operatorname{tr}(AB)=\operatorname{tr}(BA)$.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Expanding entries and exchanging the finite sums,</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\operatorname{tr}(AB)=\sum_i\sum_jA_{ij}B_{ji}
=\sum_j\sum_iB_{ji}A_{ij}=\operatorname{tr}(BA).$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S038 · Q2.2.8 Can a commutator equal the identity? / 矩阵交换子能否等于单位阵 （Page 36）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 是否存在 $n\times n$ 方阵 $A,B$，使 $AB-BA=I_n$？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Can $n\times n$ matrices $A,B$ satisfy $AB-BA=I_n$?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>No over a field of characteristic zero. Taking traces gives $\operatorname{tr}(AB-BA)=0$, while $\operatorname{tr}(I_n)=n\ne0$, a contradiction.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S039 · Q2.2.9 Product of probability matrices / 概率矩阵的乘积 （Page 36）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 若矩阵元素非负且每行之和为 $1$，称其为概率矩阵。证明两个概率矩阵的乘积仍是概率矩阵。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> A probability matrix has nonnegative entries and every row sums to $1$. Show that the product of two probability matrices is again a probability matrix.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>If $A,B$ are such matrices, every entry of $AB$ is a sum of nonnegative products. With $\mathbf1$ the all-ones vector, $B\mathbf1=\mathbf1$ and hence $(AB)\mathbf1=A\mathbf1=\mathbf1$. Thus each row of $AB$ also sums to $1$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S040 · Q2.2.10 Complete the correlation matrix again / 再论相关矩阵补全 （Page 36）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 求所有使
$$\begin{pmatrix}1&0.6&-0.3\\0.6&1&\rho\\-0.3&\rho&1\end{pmatrix}$$
成为相关矩阵的 $\rho$。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Find all $\rho$ for which $\begin{pmatrix}1&0.6&-0.3\\0.6&1&\rho\\-0.3&\rho&1\end{pmatrix}$ is a correlation matrix.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Positive semidefiniteness requires $0.55-0.36\rho-\rho^2\ge0$. Therefore</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{\frac{-9-4\sqrt{91}}{50}\le\rho\le\frac{-9+4\sqrt{91}}{50}}.$$</p>
<p>This is the same formal question as First Look Q5; the inclusive endpoints correspond to singular but valid correlation matrices.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="section-anchor" id="stefanica-finance" aria-hidden="true"></div>
~~~

== D. Financial Instruments

=== S041 · Q2.3.1 Put-option convexity arbitrage / 看跌期权凸性套利 （Page 37）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 其他条件相同、执行价为 $\$40,\$50,\$70$ 的看跌期权分别报价 $\$10,\$20,\$30$。是否存在套利？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Otherwise identical puts with strikes $\$40,\$50,\$70$ cost $\$10,\$20,\$30$. Is there an arbitrage?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Put prices must be convex in strike. Since $50=\tfrac23(40)+\tfrac13(70)$, no arbitrage requires $P(50)\le\tfrac23P(40)+\tfrac13P(70)=50/3$. It is instead $20$. Buy two $K=40$ puts and one $K=70$ put, and short three $K=50$ puts. This receives $\$10$ initially, while convexity of $(K-S_T)^+$ makes the terminal payoff nonnegative in every state.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S042 · Q2.3.2 One-period price of an ATM put / 单期模型中的平值看跌期权 （Page 37）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 股票现价 $\$50$，三个月后只可能为 $\$47$ 或 $\$52$；两种状态的真实概率各为 $50\%$。假设无股息、利率为零，平值看跌期权值多少？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> A stock is $\$50$ and in three months will be either $\$47$ or $\$52$, each with physical probability $50\%$. With no dividends and zero rates, value an at-the-money put.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>The risk-neutral up probability $q$ solves $50=52q+47(1-q)$, so $q=3/5$. The put pays $0$ up and $3$ down. Its no-arbitrage value is</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{(1-q)3=\frac65=\$1.20}.$$</p>
<p>The physical $50/50$ probabilities are irrelevant to replication.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S043 · Q2.3.3 Physical probabilities and option value / 真实概率是否影响期权价格 （Page 37）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 股票现价 $\$50$，三个月后为 $\$60$ 或 $\$40$。平值看跌期权当前价格为 $\$4$。若真实上涨概率从 $50\%$ 改为 $75\%$，期权价值如何变化？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> A $\$50$ stock will be $\$60$ or $\$40$ in three months, and its ATM put is quoted at $\$4$. If the physical up probability changes from $50\%$ to $75\%$, how does the put value change?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>It does not change merely because the physical probabilities change. No-arbitrage pricing uses the replicating portfolio, equivalently risk-neutral probabilities fixed by traded asset prices. In the stated zero-rate two-state model the unique risk-neutral up probability is $1/2$, which would imply a model value of $\$5$; thus the quoted $\$4$ is not consistent with that frictionless complete model, but changing only the physical probability still does not alter its arbitrage price.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S044 · Q2.3.4 Risk-neutral pricing / 风险中性定价 （Page 37）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 什么是风险中性定价？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What is risk-neutral pricing?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>In an arbitrage-free market, choose an equivalent measure $Q$ under which discounted tradable asset prices are martingales. A replicable payoff $H$ then has price</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$V_t=B_t\,\mathbb E^Q\!\left[\frac{H}{B_T}\middle|\mathcal F_t\right].$$</p>
<p>The measure changes probabilities, not investor preferences. In a complete market $Q$ and the replicating price are unique.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S045 · Q2.3.5 Route to the Black–Scholes formula / Black–Scholes 公式的推导路线 （Page 37）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 简述如何得到 Black–Scholes 公式。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Briefly describe how to obtain the Black–Scholes formula.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Assume GBM dynamics, apply Itô's lemma to $V(t,S)$, delta hedge to remove diffusion risk, and impose the risk-free return to obtain the Black–Scholes PDE. Solve the PDE with terminal condition $V(T,S)=(S-K)^+$, or equivalently take the discounted risk-neutral expectation with $S_T$ lognormal. For a continuous dividend yield $q$,</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$C=S_0e^{-qT}\Phi(d_1)-Ke^{-rT}\Phi(d_2),$$</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$d_{1,2}=\frac{\log(S_0/K)+(r-q\pm\tfrac12\sigma^2)T}{\sigma\sqrt T}.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S046 · Q2.3.6 Price a three-month ATM put / 三个月平值看跌期权定价 （Page 37）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 标的现价 $\$40$、波动率 $30\%$，求三个月平值看跌期权价格。假设无股息、利率为零。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Price a three-month ATM put on a non-dividend-paying asset at $\$40$ with volatility $30\%$ and zero rates.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Here $S_0=K=40$, $T=0.25$, and $d_1=0.075$, $d_2=-0.075$. Thus</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$P=40\bigl[\Phi(0.075)-\Phi(-0.075)\bigr]
=40\bigl[2\Phi(0.075)-1\bigr]\approx\boxed{\$2.39}.$$</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S047 · Q2.3.7 A stock doubles in one day / 股票一日翻倍 （Page 38）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 股票价格一天内翻倍，看涨期权价值会增加多少？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> If a stock price doubles in one day, by how much does a call option on it increase?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>There is not enough information for a number: strike, maturity, volatility, rates, dividends, and the post-move implied volatility matter. For a small move, $\Delta C\approx\Delta\,\Delta S+\tfrac12\Gamma(\Delta S)^2$, but a doubling is not a small-move setting. Static no-arbitrage only gives broad bounds such as $0\le C\le S$ and, for a fixed parameter surface, a call's slope with respect to spot lies between $0$ and the prepaid-forward discount factor.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S048 · Q2.3.8 Bounds on delta / Delta 的取值范围 （Page 38）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 期权 Delta 的最小值和最大值是什么？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What are the smallest and largest values an option delta can take?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>For standard European options on a non-dividend-paying asset, call delta lies in $[0,1]$ and put delta in $[-1,0]$. With continuous yield $q$, the bounds scale to $[0,e^{-qT}]$ and $[-e^{-qT},0]$. Arbitrary exotic or leveraged payoffs need not respect $[-1,1]$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S049 · Q2.3.9 Delta of ATM calls and puts / 平值看涨与看跌的 Delta （Page 38）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 平值看涨与平值看跌期权的 Delta 分别是多少？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What are the deltas of an at-the-money call and put?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>In Black–Scholes, $\Delta_C=e^{-qT}\Phi(d_1)$ and $\Delta_P=e^{-qT}(\Phi(d_1)-1)$. They are approximately $+1/2$ and $-1/2$ for an ATM-forward option with modest carry and volatility. They are not exactly those numbers for every definition of “ATM”; for $S=K$, $d_1=[(r-q)+\sigma^2/2]\sqrt T/\sigma$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S050 · Q2.3.10 Put–call parity / 看涨看跌平价 （Page 38）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 写出并证明欧式期权的看涨看跌平价。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> State and prove European put–call parity.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>For equal strike and maturity,</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{C-P=S_0e^{-qT}-Ke^{-rT}}.$$</p>
<p>At expiry, long call plus cash $K$ has payoff $\max(S_T,K)$; long put plus one share has the same payoff. Equal terminal payoffs must have equal current prices, which gives the identity.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S051 · Q2.3.11 Where call time value is largest / 看涨期权时间价值何处最大 （Page 38）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 证明欧式看涨期权的时间价值在平值附近最大。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Show that a European call's time value is largest at the money.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Under zero rates and dividends, time value is $C(S)-(S-K)^+$. Below $K$ its derivative is $\Delta_C&gt;0$; above $K$ its derivative is $\Delta_C-1&lt;0$. It therefore peaks at $S=K$. With nonzero carry, the precise peak depends on the convention for intrinsic value and is naturally stated near the ATM-forward level.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S052 · Q2.3.12 Implied volatility, smile and skew / 隐含波动率、微笑与偏斜 （Page 38）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 什么是隐含波动率、波动率微笑和波动率偏斜？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What are implied volatility, a volatility smile, and a volatility skew?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Implied volatility is the volatility input that makes a pricing model match an observed option price. Plotting it against strike for a fixed maturity gives the smile: both wings may sit above the center. A skew is an asymmetric slope, commonly with lower-strike equity options carrying higher implied volatility. These shapes summarize departures from constant-volatility Black–Scholes assumptions.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S053 · Q2.3.13 Gamma and convexity / Gamma 与凸性 （Page 38）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 什么是期权 Gamma？为何交易者有时偏好较小的 Gamma？为何普通欧式看涨、看跌期权的 Gamma 为正？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What is gamma? Why can small gamma be preferable, and why is gamma positive for plain-vanilla calls and puts?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Gamma is $\Gamma=\partial^2V/\partial S^2=\partial\Delta/\partial S$. Small absolute gamma makes delta more stable and reduces discrete-rehedging exposure and turnover. Vanilla call and put payoffs are convex in $S_T$; expectation and discounting preserve convexity, so their prices are convex in spot and gamma is nonnegative. In Black–Scholes, $\Gamma=e^{-qT}\phi(d_1)/(S\sigma\sqrt T)&gt;0$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S054 · Q2.3.14 When call and put values coincide / 看涨与看跌何时同价 （Page 38）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 同标的、同行权价、同到期日的欧式看涨与看跌期权何时同价？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> When do otherwise identical European calls and puts have equal value?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Put–call parity gives $C=P$ exactly when</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$S_0e^{-qT}=Ke^{-rT},\qquad\text{equivalently}\qquad F_{0,T}=K.$$</p>
<p>At the forward-money strike the discounted expected upside and downside around $K$ balance.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S055 · Q2.3.15 Scale volatility across horizons / 跨期限换算波动率 （Page 38）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 若资产六个月收益的总波动率为 $30\%$，两年收益的总波动率是多少？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> If an asset's six-month horizon volatility is $30\%$, what is its two-year horizon volatility?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Under independent, stationary increments, standard deviation scales with the square root of time:</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\sigma_{2\mathrm y}=30\%\sqrt{\frac{2}{0.5}}=\boxed{60\%}.$$</p>
<p>If “$30\%$ volatility” were already an annualized quote, the annualized number would remain $30\%$; the question uses horizon volatility.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S056 · Q2.3.16 Value an interest-rate swap / 利率互换估值 （Page 39）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何给利率互换估值？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you value an interest-rate swap?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Value each remaining leg from the current discount and forward curves. For a receive-fixed swap,</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$V=N\!\left[K\sum_i\alpha_iP(0,T_i)+P(0,T_n)-P(0,T_0)\right],$$</p>
<p>with the last expression adjusted for the already-fixed next floating coupon when valuation is between reset dates. Equivalently, it is the value of a fixed-rate bond minus a floating-rate note; pay-fixed has the opposite sign.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S057 · Q2.3.17 Ten-year zero and a ten-basis-point move / 十年零息债与十个基点 （Page 39）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 十年期零息债收益率上升 $10$ 个基点，价格约变化多少？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> By approximately how much does a ten-year zero-coupon bond price change when its yield rises by ten basis points?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Its modified duration is approximately $10$ under continuous compounding. Thus</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\frac{\Delta P}{P}\approx-D\,\Delta y=-10(0.001)=-1\%.$$</p>
<p>Exactly under continuous compounding, $P_{\rm new}/P_{\rm old}=e^{-0.01}\approx0.99005$, a $0.995\%$ fall.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S058 · Q2.3.18 Bond price from duration / 用久期估算债券价格 （Page 39）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 一只五年期债券价格为 $102$，久期为 $3.5$ 年。若收益率下降 $50$ 个基点，估算新价格。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> A five-year bond priced at $102$ has duration $3.5$. Estimate its price after a fifty-basis-point yield decrease.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p class="equation-line">$$\Delta P\approx-PD\,\Delta y=-102(3.5)(-0.005)=1.785.$$</p>
<p>The estimated new price is $\boxed{103.785}$. Convexity would refine this first-order estimate.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S059 · Q2.3.19 Forward contracts and forward prices / 远期合约与远期价格 （Page 39）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 什么是远期合约？什么是远期价格？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What is a forward contract, and what is the forward price?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>A forward is an agreement today to exchange an asset at time $T$ for a delivery price $K$. The forward price $F_{0,T}$ is the delivery price that makes a new contract worth zero. For an asset with continuous yield $q$ and deterministic rate $r$,</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\boxed{F_{0,T}=S_0e^{(r-q)T}}.$$</p>
<p>The value later is not the same object as the forward price.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S060 · Q2.3.20 Treasury and commodity forwards / 国债与商品远期定价 （Page 39）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 国债远期与商品远期的价格如何确定？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How are forward prices determined for Treasury securities and commodities?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Cash-and-carry gives the future value of net spot carrying cost. If $I$ is the present value of coupons paid before delivery, a Treasury forward satisfies</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$F_{0,T}=(S_0-I)e^{rT}.$$</p>
<p>For a commodity, add the present value $U$ of storage and other costs and subtract the present value of convenience yield $Y$:</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$F_{0,T}=(S_0+U-Y)e^{rT},$$</p>
<p>or $S_0e^{(r+u-y)T}$ under continuous proportional rates.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S061 · Q2.3.21 Eurodollar futures / Eurodollar 期货 （Page 39）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 什么是 Eurodollar 期货？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What is a Eurodollar futures contract?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Historically it was a cash-settled futures contract on the three-month USD LIBOR rate for a future accrual period, quoted as $100-L$, where $L$ is the annualized rate in percent. A one-basis-point move was worth $\$25$ per $\$1$ million notional. LIBOR cessation has moved current markets to SOFR futures, but this is the instrument meant by the book.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S062 · Q2.3.22 Forwards versus futures / 远期与期货的区别 （Page 39）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 远期合约与期货合约的主要区别是什么？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What are the main differences between forwards and futures?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Forwards are typically OTC, customizable, settled at maturity, and expose each party to bilateral counterparty risk. Futures are standardized and exchange-cleared, margined, marked to market daily, and usually more liquid. Daily settlement can make a futures price differ from a forward price when rates are stochastic and correlated with the underlying.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S063 · Q2.3.23 Scale VaR across time and confidence / 跨期限与置信度换算 VaR （Page 39）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 某组合五日 $98\%$ VaR 为 $\$10$ million。在独立正态收益与平方根时间规则下，十日 $99\%$ VaR 是多少？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> A portfolio has five-day $98\%$ VaR of $\$10$ million. Under normal independent returns and square-root-of-time scaling, what is its ten-day $99\%$ VaR?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Scale both the horizon and the normal quantile:</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$\operatorname{VaR}_{10,99\%}
=10\,\text{m}\times\sqrt{\frac{10}{5}}\times
\frac{\Phi^{-1}(0.99)}{\Phi^{-1}(0.98)}
\approx\boxed{\$16.0\text{ million}}.$$</p>
<p>This calculation is only as valid as the normal-i.i.d. approximation.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S064 · Q2.3.24 Two put prices / 两个看跌期权报价 （Page 39）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 同标的、同到期日的执行价 $\$30$ 与 $\$20$ 看跌期权分别报价 $\$6$ 与 $\$4$。能否仅凭这些报价构造套利？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Puts with strikes $\$30$ and $\$20$ cost $\$6$ and $\$4$, with the same underlying and maturity. Do these prices alone imply an arbitrage?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>No. The $20$–$30$ put spread costs $2$ and has payoff between $0$ and $10$, so monotonicity and the vertical-spread upper bound are respected. Convexity using the zero-strike put gives $P(20)\le(2/3)P(30)=4$, here exactly. Additional spot, rate, or other-strike information could add constraints, but the two quotes alone are arbitrage-consistent.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S065 · Q2.3.25 Implied versus realized volatility / 隐含波动率与实现波动率 （Page 40）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 以 $28\%$ 隐含波动率卖出一个月看跌期权，并持续做 Delta 对冲；到期后实现波动率为 $16\%$。赚了还是亏了？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> You sell a one-month put at $28\%$ implied volatility and delta-hedge continuously. Realized volatility is $16\%$. Did you make or lose money?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>In the ideal diffusion model with consistent rates, no jumps, continuous frictionless hedging, and the same volatility definition, the short option earns because the sold variance exceeds realized variance. The hedged P&amp;L is approximately a gamma-weighted integral proportional to $\int(\sigma_{\rm imp}^2-\sigma_{\rm realized}^2)S_t^2\Gamma_t\,dt&gt;0$. A single realized-volatility statistic does not guarantee profit in real markets: jumps, skew moves, discrete hedging, transaction costs, and path-dependent gamma weighting can reverse it.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S066 · Q2.3.26 The zero-cost call replication fallacy / 零成本复制看涨期权的谬误 （Page 40）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 标的现价 $\$25$，看涨期权执行价 $\$30$。有人声称：价格每次上穿 $\$30$ 就以 $\$30$ 买一股，下穿时再以 $\$30$ 卖出，因此可零成本复制到期收益。错在哪里？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> A proposed replication of a $K=\$30$ call buys one share whenever spot crosses above $\$30$ and sells it whenever spot crosses below, apparently always trading at $\$30$ and producing the call payoff for free. What is wrong?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>A continuous diffusion can cross a level infinitely often; the indicator hedge $1_{\{S_t&gt;K\}}$ has unbounded turnover and is not an admissible finite-variation, self-financing strategy. Transaction costs explode in any realistic implementation. Mathematically, Tanaka's formula shows the missing term:</p>
<p class="equation-line">$$(S_T-K)^+=(S_0-K)^++\int_0^T1_{\{S_t&gt;K\}}\,dS_t+\frac12L_T^K,$$</p>
<p>where the positive local-time term $L_T^K/2$ is exactly what the informal argument ignores.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="section-anchor" id="stefanica-cpp" aria-hidden="true"></div>
~~~

== E. C\+\+ & Data Structures

=== S067 · Q2.4.1 Declare an array / 声明数组 （Page 41）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 在 C++ 中如何声明数组？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you declare an array in C++?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>int raw[10]{};                 // built-in fixed-size array
std::array&lt;int, 10&gt; fixed{};  // safer fixed-size container
std::vector&lt;int&gt; dynamic(10); // runtime-sized container</code></pre>
<p>The size of a built-in array must normally be a compile-time constant in standard C++.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S068 · Q2.4.2 Address of a variable / 取得变量地址 （Page 41）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何取得变量的地址？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you obtain the address of a variable?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>int x = 7;
int* p = &amp;x;          // or std::addressof(x)</code></pre>
<p>Dereferencing $p$ with <code>*p</code> accesses $x$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S069 · Q2.4.3 Array of pointers / 指针数组 （Page 41）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何声明一个指针数组？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you declare an array of pointers?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>int* pointers[10]{};                 // ten pointers to int
std::array&lt;int*, 10&gt; pointers2{};</code></pre>
<p>Parentheses change the declaration: <code>int (*p)[10]</code> is instead a pointer to an array of ten integers.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S070 · Q2.4.4 Const pointer forms / const 指针的三种形式 （Page 41）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何声明常量指针、指向常量的指针，以及指向常量的常量指针？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you declare a const pointer, a pointer to const, and a const pointer to const?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>int* const fixed_pointer = &amp;x;             // pointer cannot change
const int* pointer_to_const = &amp;x;          // pointee cannot change through it
const int* const fixed_pointer_to_const = &amp;x; // neither can change</code></pre>
<p><code>int const*</code> and <code>const int*</code> mean the same thing.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S071 · Q2.4.5 Dynamic array / 动态数组 （Page 41）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何声明动态数组？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you declare a dynamic array?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>std::vector&lt;int&gt; a(n);               // preferred
auto a2 = std::make_unique&lt;int[]&gt;(n); // owning array pointer</code></pre>
<p>Legacy <code>new int[n]</code> must be paired with <code>delete[]</code>; RAII containers and smart pointers prevent leaks and exception-safety errors.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S072 · Q2.4.6 Function signature / 函数签名 （Page 41）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> C++ 函数声明的一般形式是什么？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What is the general form of a C++ function signature?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>ReturnType function_name(ParameterType1 p1, ParameterType2 p2)
    cv_qualifier ref_qualifier noexcept_specifier;</code></pre>
<p>For overload resolution, the signature is determined by the function name and parameter-type list (plus relevant member/template qualifiers), not merely by the return type.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S073 · Q2.4.7 Pass by reference / 按引用传递 （Page 41）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何按引用传递参数？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you pass an argument by reference?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>void increment(int&amp; x) { ++x; }</code></pre>
<p>The function receives an alias and can modify the caller's object. Use a pointer when null or reseating is part of the interface.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S074 · Q2.4.8 Read-only reference argument / 只读引用参数 （Page 41）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何通过引用传递只读参数？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you pass a read-only argument by reference?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>void print(const LargeObject&amp; value);</code></pre>
<p>A const lvalue reference avoids a copy, prevents mutation through the parameter, and can bind to temporaries.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S075 · Q2.4.9 Pointer versus reference / 指针与引用 （Page 41）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 指针和引用有哪些重要区别？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What are the important differences between pointers and references?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>A pointer is an object that can be null, reseated, copied, compared, and used in pointer arithmetic; access needs explicit dereferencing. A reference is an alias that must be bound at initialization and cannot later be reseated, so it normally expresses a required object. Neither construct guarantees lifetime safety: both can dangle.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S076 · Q2.4.10 Default parameter / 默认参数 （Page 41）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何为函数参数设置默认值？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you set a default value for a parameter?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>void log(std::string_view message, int level = 1);</code></pre>
<p>After a parameter has a default, later parameters must also have defaults. Put the default in one visible declaration, normally the header, not again in the definition.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S077 · Q2.4.11 Template function / 函数模板 （Page 41）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何创建函数模板？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you create a function template?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>template&lt;typename T&gt;
T maximum(const T&amp; a, const T&amp; b) {
    return b &lt; a ? a : b;
}</code></pre>
<p>The compiler instantiates the function for types satisfying the operations used; modern C++ can state those requirements with a concept.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S078 · Q2.4.12 Pointer to a function / 函数指针 （Page 42）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何声明函数指针？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you declare a pointer to a function?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>double (*operation)(double, double) = &amp;add;
using Operation = double (*)(double, double);</code></pre>
<p><code>std::function</code> is more flexible when type-erased stateful callables are required, at some runtime cost.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S079 · Q2.4.13 Prevent implicit conversion / 禁止隐式类型转换 （Page 42）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何防止编译器利用类的构造函数做隐式转换？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you prevent implicit conversion through a class constructor?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>class Price {
public:
    explicit Price(double value) : value_(value) {}
private:
    double value_;
};</code></pre>
<p>The <code>explicit</code> specifier also applies to conversion operators and, in modern C++, may be conditional.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S080 · Q2.4.14 Uses of the static keyword / static 关键字的用途 （Page 42）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 说明 C++ 关键字 <code>static</code> 的各种用途。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Describe the uses of <code>static</code> in C++.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>A block-scope static has static storage duration but local scope and is initialized once. A static data member is shared by all objects; a static member function has no <code>this</code> pointer. At namespace scope, <code>static</code> gives internal linkage, though an anonymous namespace is usually preferred. Static storage-duration objects live for the program's lifetime.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S081 · Q2.4.15 Can a static member function be const? / 静态成员函数能否为 const （Page 42）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 静态成员函数可以声明为 <code>const</code> 吗？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Can a static member function be const-qualified?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>No. A member-function <code>const</code> qualifier constrains the object reached through <code>this</code>. A static member function has no <code>this</code> pointer and is not invoked on a particular object.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S082 · Q2.4.16 Constructor initializer lists / 构造函数初始化列表 （Page 42）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 构造函数何时必须或应当使用初始化列表，而不是在函数体内赋值？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> When is a constructor initializer list required or preferable to assignment in the constructor body?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>It is required for references, const members, base classes, and members without an accessible default constructor. It is generally preferable because it constructs each subobject directly instead of default-constructing and then assigning. Actual initialization order follows member declaration order, not list order.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S083 · Q2.4.17 Copy constructor and pointer members / 拷贝构造与指针成员 （Page 42）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 什么是拷贝构造函数？类中有指针成员时，默认拷贝构造为什么可能出错？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What is a copy constructor, and why can the default copy constructor be dangerous for pointer data members?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>A copy constructor typically has the form <code>T(const T&amp; other)</code>. The generated version copies members individually, so a raw owning pointer is shallow-copied: two objects then own the same allocation, causing aliasing, double deletion, or dangling pointers. Prefer value members and RAII smart pointers; otherwise implement the Rule of Five with a deep copy or explicitly disable copying.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S084 · Q2.4.18 Shallow-copy code output / 浅拷贝程序的输出 （Page 42）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 题中类 <code>A</code> 含有 <code>int* ptr</code>，并在析构函数中执行 <code>delete ptr</code>。主函数令 <code>aa.ptr = new int(2)</code>，把 <code>aa</code> 按值传入空函数 <code>foo</code>，随后输出 <code>*aa.ptr</code>。程序会输出什么？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Class <code>A</code> contains <code>int* ptr</code> and executes <code>delete ptr</code> in its destructor. Main sets <code>aa.ptr = new int(2)</code>, passes <code>aa</code> by value to an empty <code>foo</code>, and then prints <code>*aa.ptr</code>. What is the output?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>There is no defined output. The implicit copy constructor shallow-copies the pointer. Destruction of <code>foo</code>'s parameter frees the allocation, so the original object holds a dangling pointer; dereferencing it is undefined behavior, and its later destructor may double-delete it. It might print garbage, appear to print $2$, or crash—none is guaranteed.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S085 · Q2.4.19 Operator overloading / 运算符重载 （Page 43）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 如何重载运算符？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> How do you overload an operator?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>struct Vec {
    double x, y;
    Vec&amp; operator+=(const Vec&amp; rhs) {
        x += rhs.x; y += rhs.y; return *this;
    }
};
Vec operator+(Vec lhs, const Vec&amp; rhs) {
    return lhs += rhs;
}</code></pre>
<p>At least one operand must be a user-defined type. Preserve the conventional meaning and algebra of the operator.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S086 · Q2.4.20 Smart pointers / 智能指针 （Page 43）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 什么是智能指针？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What are smart pointers?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Smart pointers are RAII ownership wrappers. <code>std::unique_ptr</code> expresses exclusive movable ownership; <code>std::shared_ptr</code> uses reference-counted shared ownership; <code>std::weak_ptr</code> observes a shared object without extending its lifetime and can break cycles. Prefer <code>std::make_unique</code> and <code>std::make_shared</code>.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S087 · Q2.4.21 Encapsulation / 封装 （Page 43）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 什么是封装？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What is encapsulation?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Encapsulation groups state with the operations that maintain its invariants and hides implementation details behind a stable interface, using access control and abstraction. It reduces coupling: callers depend on behavior rather than data representation.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S088 · Q2.4.22 Polymorphism / 多态 （Page 43）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 什么是多态？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What is polymorphism?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Polymorphism lets one interface represent multiple implementations. Runtime polymorphism uses virtual dispatch through a base pointer or reference. Compile-time polymorphism uses overloads, templates, and concepts. Value-oriented alternatives such as <code>std::variant</code> can avoid inheritance when the set of types is closed.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S089 · Q2.4.23 Inheritance / 继承 （Page 43）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 什么是继承？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What is inheritance?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Inheritance defines a derived class from a base class, reusing or refining behavior and, with public inheritance, expressing an “is-a” substitutability relationship. Prefer composition for mere code reuse; public inheritance should respect the base contract and Liskov substitution.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S090 · Q2.4.24 Virtual and pure virtual functions / 虚函数与纯虚函数 （Page 43）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 什么是虚函数和纯虚函数？何时使用纯虚函数？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> What are virtual and pure virtual functions, and when do you use a pure virtual function?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>A virtual function dispatches according to the dynamic type when called through a base pointer or reference. A pure virtual declaration such as <code>virtual double value() const = 0;</code> makes the class abstract and requires concrete derived classes to supply the interface, unless they remain abstract. Use <code>override</code> on overrides.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S091 · Q2.4.25 Virtual destructors and constructors / 虚析构函数与构造函数 （Page 43）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 为什么基类析构函数常要声明为虚函数？构造函数可以是虚函数吗？</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Why are destructors often virtual in base classes? Can constructors be virtual?</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>If an object may be deleted through a base pointer, the base destructor must be virtual so the derived destructor runs; otherwise behavior is undefined. Constructors cannot be virtual because dynamic type construction is not complete during base construction. A virtual <code>clone</code> or factory function supplies polymorphic construction.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S092 · Q2.4.26 Factorial function / 阶乘函数 （Page 44）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 编写函数计算正整数的阶乘。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Write a function that computes the factorial of a positive integer.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>std::uint64_t factorial(unsigned n) {
    std::uint64_t result = 1;
    for (unsigned k = 2; k &lt;= n; ++k) {
        if (result &gt; UINT64_MAX / k) throw std::overflow_error("factorial");
        result *= k;
    }
    return result;
}</code></pre>
<p>This also defines $0!=1$ and detects fixed-width overflow.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S093 · Q2.4.27 Maximum-sum subarray / 最大子数组和 （Page 44）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 编写函数，返回数组中元素和最大的连续子数组。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Write a function that returns a contiguous subarray having maximum sum.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>Kadane's algorithm can retain the actual interval as well as its sum. The half-open interval <code>[begin,end)</code> returned below is nonempty:</p>
<pre><code>struct MaxSubarray {
    long long sum;
    std::size_t begin;
    std::size_t end;
};

MaxSubarray max_subarray(const std::vector&lt;long long&gt;&amp; a) {
    if (a.empty()) throw std::invalid_argument("empty array");

    long long ending_sum = a[0];
    long long best_sum = a[0];
    std::size_t ending_begin = 0;
    std::size_t best_begin = 0;
    std::size_t best_end = 1;

    for (std::size_t i = 1; i &lt; a.size(); ++i) {
        if (ending_sum &lt; 0) {
            ending_sum = a[i];
            ending_begin = i;
        } else {
            ending_sum += a[i];
        }
        if (ending_sum &gt; best_sum) {
            best_sum = ending_sum;
            best_begin = ending_begin;
            best_end = i + 1;
        }
    }
    return {best_sum, best_begin, best_end};
}</code></pre>
<p>The subarray is <code>a[begin]</code> through <code>a[end-1]</code>. Time is $O(n)$ and extra space is $O(1)$, excluding the returned view or copied elements.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S094 · Q2.4.28 Prime factors / 质因数分解 （Page 44）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 编写函数返回正整数的全部质因数（含重数）。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Write a function returning the prime factors of a positive integer, including multiplicities.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>std::vector&lt;std::uint64_t&gt; factors(std::uint64_t n) {
    std::vector&lt;std::uint64_t&gt; out;
    for (std::uint64_t p = 2; p &lt;= n / p; ++p)
        while (n % p == 0) { out.push_back(p); n /= p; }
    if (n &gt; 1) out.push_back(n);
    return out;
}</code></pre>
<p>Trial division takes $O(\sqrt n)$ divisions in the worst case.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S095 · Q2.4.29 Swap two bits / 交换两个二进制位 （Page 44）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 编写函数，交换一个 $64$ 位整数的第 $i$ 位和第 $j$ 位。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Write a function that swaps bits $i$ and $j$ of a 64-bit integer.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>std::uint64_t swap_bits(std::uint64_t x, unsigned i, unsigned j) {
    const auto different = ((x &gt;&gt; i) ^ (x &gt;&gt; j)) &amp; 1ULL;
    return different ? x ^ ((1ULL &lt;&lt; i) | (1ULL &lt;&lt; j)) : x;
}</code></pre>
<p>Require $i,j&lt;64$ to avoid an invalid shift.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S096 · Q2.4.30 Reverse a singly linked list / 反转单链表 （Page 44）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 编写函数反转单链表。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Write a function that reverses a singly linked list.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>Node* reverse(Node* head) {
    Node* previous = nullptr;
    while (head) {
        Node* next = head-&gt;next;
        head-&gt;next = previous;
        previous = head;
        head = next;
    }
    return previous;
}</code></pre>
<p>Time is $O(n)$ and extra space is $O(1)$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S097 · Q2.4.31 Balanced parentheses / 括号匹配 （Page 44）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 编写函数，判断字符串中的括号是否平衡。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Write a function that returns whether the parentheses in a string are balanced.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<p>For one bracket type, scan with a counter: increment on <code>(</code>, decrement on <code>)</code>, reject if it becomes negative, and accept only if it ends at zero. For <code>()[]{}</code>, push opening brackets onto a stack and require every closer to match the top. Both versions are $O(n)$; the general version uses $O(n)$ worst-case space.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S098 · Q2.4.32 Height of a binary tree / 二叉树高度 （Page 44）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 编写函数返回任意二叉树的高度。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Write a function returning the height of an arbitrary binary tree.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>int height(const Node* node) {
    if (!node) return 0;
    return 1 + std::max(height(node-&gt;left), height(node-&gt;right));
}</code></pre>
<p>This convention counts nodes on the longest root-to-leaf path. Time is $O(n)$ and recursion space $O(h)$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S099 · Q2.4.33 Fibonacci number / Fibonacci 数 （Page 44）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 编写 C++ 函数计算第 $n$ 个 Fibonacci 数。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Write a C++ function computing the $n$-th Fibonacci number.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>std::uint64_t fibonacci(unsigned n) {
    if (n == 0) return 0;
    std::uint64_t previous = 0;
    std::uint64_t current = 1;
    for (unsigned k = 1; k &lt; n; ++k) {
        if (UINT64_MAX - previous &lt; current)
            throw std::overflow_error("fibonacci");
        const auto next = previous + current;
        previous = current;
        current = next;
    }
    return current;
}</code></pre>
<p>This uses $F_0=0,F_1=1$, runs in $O(n)$ time and $O(1)$ space. Fast doubling reduces time to $O(\log n)$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

=== S100 · Q2.4.34 Basic calculator / 基础表达式计算器 （Page 44）
~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="bilingual-question">
<p><strong>中文:</strong> 实现一个计算器，求只含非负整数、空格、加减号和圆括号的合法表达式之值；不可调用 <code>eval</code>。</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Evaluate a valid expression containing nonnegative integers, spaces, plus and minus signs, and parentheses, without using <code>eval</code>.</p>
</div>
<details class="answer"><summary>Solution</summary><div class="answer-content">
<pre><code>long long calculate(std::string_view s) {
    long long result = 0, number = 0, sign = 1;
    std::vector&lt;long long&gt; stack;
    for (char c : s) {
        if (std::isdigit(static_cast&lt;unsigned char&gt;(c))) {
            number = 10 * number + (c - '0');
        } else if (c == '+' || c == '-') {
            result += sign * number; number = 0;
            sign = (c == '+') ? 1 : -1;
        } else if (c == '(') {
            stack.push_back(result); stack.push_back(sign);
            result = 0; sign = 1;
        } else if (c == ')') {
            result += sign * number; number = 0;
            const auto outer_sign = stack.back(); stack.pop_back();
            const auto outer_value = stack.back(); stack.pop_back();
            result = outer_value + outer_sign * result;
        }
    }
    return result + sign * number;
}</code></pre>
<p>Each character is processed once, so time and worst-case stack space are $O(n)$.</p>
</div></details>
~~~

